    <detaileddescription>
<para>Algorithms for parallel sorting.</para><para>These algorithms use multiple threads to sort large arrays of values in parallel. Their usage is similar to std::sort in terms of the arguments, but they also take an additional argument to specify the number of threads. The following algorithms are implemented:</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para><ref refid="namespaceRose_1_1ParallelSort_1ad2cf3da4a1f6d16ce3821089158ec290" kindref="member">quicksort()</ref> </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
